---
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import siteConfig from '~/config/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms"
  heading="Terms"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  intro="The ordinary terms that come with a portfolio site."
  description={`Terms of use for ${siteConfig.name}.`}
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Terms' }]}
>
  <section class="wrap sec" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="prose rev">
      <p class="form-note">
        <strong>Template — replace before you publish.</strong> This page is a starting
        point written for the demo site, not legal advice. Edit it in
        <code>src/pages/terms.astro</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>Using this site</h2>
      <p>
        This is a portfolio. You are welcome to read it, link to it and quote from it with
        attribution. Republishing whole pages as your own is not welcome.
      </p>

      <h2>The work shown here</h2>
      <p>
        Case studies describe demo projects created for this theme. On a real deployment,
        replace this paragraph with a note about which work is shown with client
        permission and who holds the rights to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        Content is published in good faith and may go out of date. Nothing here is a
        contractual offer; scope and price are agreed in writing before any work starts.
      </p>

      <h2>Links out</h2>
      <p>
        External links are provided for convenience. The sites they point at are not under
        this site's control and are not its responsibility.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided as is. To the extent the law allows, no liability is accepted
        for loss arising from its use. Local consumer law may give you rights that cannot
        be excluded, and nothing here limits those.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Send them to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.email}`}>{siteConfig.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
